From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 19:53:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: csiphy: add a module parameter to sweep
 the settle count

The computed settle count is not obviously right and the only way to judge it
is to look at the image, so make it sweepable without a rebuild.

That is how the current default was confirmed. Measured on msm8998 hardware
2026-08-20: at the computed 11 (685 MHz rear link, 200 MHz settle timer) the
frame carries 1-2 stray wrong-coloured pixels, and forcing 14 -- the value
stock Android programs for this PHY -- made the artefacts visibly WORSE. A
settle count is wrong in both directions, and the vendor numbers evidently do
not transfer to this link rate and lane configuration. So the computed value
stays the default and the override stays at 0.

The remaining 1-2 stray pixels are unexplained; this knob is the tool for
whoever chases them.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 .../qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c         | 22 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c
index 576d02670b40..08a5cd129ffd 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c
@@ -831,6 +831,22 @@ static irqreturn_t csiphy_isr(int irq, void *dev)
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Sweep the settle count without a rebuild; 0 keeps the computed value.
+ *
+ * Worth having because the computed value is not obviously right and the only
+ * way to judge it is to look at the image. Measured on msm8998 2026-08-20: the
+ * computed 11 (685 MHz rear link, 200 MHz settle timer) leaves 1-2 stray
+ * wrong-coloured pixels per frame, and forcing the vendor's 14 -- the value
+ * stock Android programs -- made it visibly WORSE, not better. So the vendor
+ * numbers do not transfer to this configuration and the computed value stays
+ * the default.
+ */
+static unsigned int settle_override;
+module_param(settle_override, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(settle_override,
+		 "CSIPHY: override the computed settle count (0: use the default)");
+
 /*
  * csiphy_settle_cnt_calc - Calculate settle count value
  *
@@ -975,7 +991,11 @@ static void csiphy_lanes_enable(struct csiphy_device *csiphy,
 	u8 val;
 	int i;
 
-	settle_cnt = csiphy_settle_cnt_calc(link_freq, csiphy->timer_clk_rate);
+	if (settle_override)
+		settle_cnt = settle_override;
+	else
+		settle_cnt = csiphy_settle_cnt_calc(link_freq,
+						    csiphy->timer_clk_rate);
 
 	val = CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRL5_CLK_ENABLE;
 	for (i = 0; i < c->num_data; i++)
